.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-record-decide 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-record\-decide \- Derive a family\*(Aqs reading, record it without echoing it, and decide over it with the named rules
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten record decide\fR [\fB\-\-input\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-rule\fR> <\fIfamily\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Derive a family\*(Aqs reading, record it without echoing it, and decide over it with the named rules
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-input\fR \fI<input>\fR
A `<key>=<value>` input this family needs beyond stdin (repeatable)
.TP
\fB\-\-rule\fR \fI<rule>\fR
The declared rule that decides over the record just written (repeatable, at least one)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIfamily\fR>
The record family, which selects the reading and is the key a module reads it under
